  "scriptId": "td-02-same-distance-speed-time-ratios",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Same Distance: Speed and Time Ratios",
    "description": "Use inverse speed-time reasoning for the same distance, including percentages, time differences, and leap-based speed comparisons.",
    "teachingApproach": "Begin with two riders covering the same route so the inverse relationship is visible. Turn speed ratios into reversed time ratios, then extend the idea to percentage speed changes, late/early time differences, and leap-frequency questions. Keep asking whether the distance is actually the same before using the inverse shortcut.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 18, Time and Distance. Approved scope: For equal distances, teach that speed and time are inversely proportional. Cover speed/time ratios, percentage increases or decreases in speed, time differences, ratio-based recovery of actual times, distance ratios when times differ, and leap-length × leap-frequency comparisons. Emphasize that the inverse shortcut is valid only when the distance is fixed."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn the shortcut that appears whenever two people cover the same distance.\n\nFor one fixed distance, moving faster means spending less time. Speed and time pull in opposite directions.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Two riders cover the same 120 km.\n\nAt 40 km/hr, time = 120 ÷ 40 = 3 hr.\nAt 60 km/hr, time = 120 ÷ 60 = 2 hr.\n\nThe faster rider takes less time.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For the same distance:\n\nSpeed ratio = 40 : 60 = 2 : 3\nTime ratio = 3 : 2\n\nSo the time ratio is the speed ratio reversed.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
        "text": "A and B cover the same distance. Their speeds are in the ratio 3 : 4. What is the ratio of their times?",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "input": {
        "type": "CHOICE",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "label": "4 : 3"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "label": "3 : 4"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "label": "7 : 4"
          },
          {
            "id": "d",
            "label": "9 : 16"
          }
        ]
      },
      "questionReference": {
