    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A percentage increase in speed does not give the same percentage decrease in time.\n\nIf speed rises by 25%, new speed = 125% = 5/4 of old speed.\n\nFor the same distance, new time = 4/5 of old time.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So if the old time was 50 minutes:\n\nNew time = 50 × 4/5 = 40 min.\n\nThe time falls by 10 minutes, which is 20% of 50 — not 25%.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
